{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1110613-fomori-enhancement","id":1110613,"title":"Fomori Enhancement...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-02T12:01:08-07:00","id":1110613,"title":"Fomori Enhancement...","content":"So bit of an odd question the Fomori power enhancement. Does the user physically transform? Or simply rewrite the targets tastes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T12:43:21-07:00","id":1110628,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what the specific power it is you are talking about, but the answer is probably &quot;whatever you need it to be.&quot; Powers for NPC antagonists can be very loose because the mechanics exist solely for the ST to run their chronicle. You don't need to worry about game balance issues like is this gift too powerful, or how much XP is this really worth because those are PC issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T13:05:20-07:00","id":1110633,"title":"","content":"The power basically says &quot;The Fomori Brain Scans a target and then the Fomori becomes their 'perfect mate'&quot; If it's the former, physical transformation. This could be used to disguise the Fomori by using it on some random person. If it's the latter, wouldn't the target notice their change in tastes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T13:36:20-07:00","id":1110646,"title":"","content":"Probably a physical transformation similar to the shapeshifting capabilities of neomah from Exalted. No one is likely to be able to give a more descriptive answer; material from the Book of the Wyrm tends to be kind of touch and go. There's a spirit Charm that hasn't been described mechanically in like over 20 years, for example, but damned if you can't still find it in the list of powers that the Dream Maker banes have, even in W20.<br /> <br /> Edit: That said, if the enticer power is actually not particularly ambiguous. If it rewrote tastes to broaden appeal, the power wouldn't need to possibly change the apparent gender of the enticer, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 07-02-2017, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T12:40:15-07:00","id":1110949,"title":"","content":"Weird. I keep thinking that this was the subject of a Star Trek episode at one point. <br /> <br /> I wonder if there could be two different types of Enticers, a lesser model that only takes on the personality traits and body language it's target finds appealing, and a greater version that can shape shift when needed. Hmm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T17:21:40-07:00","id":1111070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1110613-fomori-enhancement?p=1110949#post1110949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weird. I keep thinking that this was the subject of a Star Trek episode at one point.<br /> <br /> I wonder if there could be two different types of Enticers, a lesser model that only takes on the personality traits and body language it's target finds appealing, and a greater version that can shape shift when needed. Hmm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Enticer has, by turns in various different books, been presented with and without Enhancement. If you're making a character, you're not under an obligation to have every power of a given fomor breed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}